            "reply_data": [
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7055955?u=1122f8f2eca984676225a9b9600d2568bff89d57&v=4",
                        "login": "abenz1267",
                        "resourcePath": "/abenz1267",
                        "url": "https://github.com/abenz1267"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "I've been trying this for a few weeks now, the default i mean, i can can only say: it's a bit annoying that you have to use enter for completion with snippets, f.e. functions, but \"normal\" completion works with simply selecting.\r\n\r\nI'd just want the completion to always behave the same ideally. I have this now:\r\n\r\n```\r\n        vim.keymap.set('i', '<C-j>', function()\r\n            return vim.fn.pumvisible() == 1 and '<DOWN>' or '<C-j>'\r\n        end, { expr = true })\r\n\r\n        vim.keymap.set('i', '<C-k>', function()\r\n            return vim.fn.pumvisible() == 1 and '<UP>' or '<C-k>'\r\n        end, { expr = true })\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhich works fine.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I've been trying this for a few weeks now, the default i mean, i can can only say: it's a bit annoying that you have to use enter for completion with snippets, f.e. functions, but \"normal\" completion works with simply selecting.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd just want the completion to always behave the same ideally. I have this now:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"        vim.keymap.set('i', '&lt;C-j&gt;', function()\n            return vim.fn.pumvisible() == 1 and '&lt;DOWN&gt;' or '&lt;C-j&gt;'\n        end, { expr = true })\n\n        vim.keymap.set('i', '&lt;C-k&gt;', function()\n            return vim.fn.pumvisible() == 1 and '&lt;UP&gt;' or '&lt;C-k&gt;'\n        end, { expr = true })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">        vim.keymap.set('i', '&lt;C-j&gt;', function()\n            return vim.fn.pumvisible() == 1 and '&lt;DOWN&gt;' or '&lt;C-j&gt;'\n        end, { expr = true })\n\n        vim.keymap.set('i', '&lt;C-k&gt;', function()\n            return vim.fn.pumvisible() == 1 and '&lt;UP&gt;' or '&lt;C-k&gt;'\n        end, { expr = true })\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">which works fine.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I've been trying this for a few weeks now, the default i mean, i can can only say: it's a bit annoying that you have to use enter for completion with snippets, f.e. functions, but \"normal\" completion works with simply selecting.\nI'd just want the completion to always behave the same ideally. I have this now:\n        vim.keymap.set('i', '<C-j>', function()\n            return vim.fn.pumvisible() == 1 and '<DOWN>' or '<C-j>'\n        end, { expr = true })\n\n        vim.keymap.set('i', '<C-k>', function()\n            return vim.fn.pumvisible() == 1 and '<UP>' or '<C-k>'\n        end, { expr = true })\n\nwhich works fine.",
