                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> it's a bit annoying that you have to use enter for completion with snippets, f.e. functions, but \"normal\" completion works with simply selecting.\r\n\r\nI am not sure what you mean here. The behavior of 'mini.completion' regarding accepting snippets is that it [works with `<C-y>` *or* any non-keyworkd character](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/126ce3328c78399dcff58272f6f540a373b62a75/doc/mini-completion.txt#L109-L111). In practice it usually means that just keep typing after selecting will expand a snippet automatically.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">it's a bit annoying that you have to use enter for completion with snippets, f.e. functions, but \"normal\" completion works with simply selecting.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I am not sure what you mean here. The behavior of 'mini.completion' regarding accepting snippets is that it <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/126ce3328c78399dcff58272f6f540a373b62a75/doc/mini-completion.txt#L109-L111\">works with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-y&gt;</code> <em>or</em> any non-keyworkd character</a>. In practice it usually means that just keep typing after selecting will expand a snippet automatically.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "it's a bit annoying that you have to use enter for completion with snippets, f.e. functions, but \"normal\" completion works with simply selecting.\n\nI am not sure what you mean here. The behavior of 'mini.completion' regarding accepting snippets is that it works with <C-y> or any non-keyworkd character. In practice it usually means that just keep typing after selecting will expand a snippet automatically.",
